  "historical_output_text": " **Subject:** How to Remove Stains from a Microwave\n\n**Forum Post:**\nHey everyone, I accidentally spilled some tomato sauce in my microwave and now there's a stubborn stain! Does anyone have a good way to clean this up? I don't want to damage my microwave.\n\n**Reply:**\n\nHi there! Dealing with stains in the microwave can be a bit tricky, but don't worry, I've got a simple and effective method you can try. Here's what you can do:\n\n1. **Make a Baking Soda and Water Paste:** Start by mixing baking soda and water to create a paste that's thick enough to stick to the stain. You want it to be a bit runny so it can spread easily.\n\n2. **Apply the Paste:** Use a soft brush or a sponge to apply the paste directly to the stain",
